---
// Claim Checker — product page.
// Visual design: the nikdesign.ca/hellogroundnews design system, verbatim
// (dark tokens, Bebas Neue / Lora / JetBrains Mono, grain, chapter layout),
// with an added light theme via [data-theme="light"] token overrides and a
// fixed theme switcher. Standalone page (no Base layout) by design.
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Claim Checker — TeamBotics</title>
    <meta name="description" content="An open method for verifying public claims against documented evidence. Published by TeamBotics Inc. under the MIT Licence." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bebas+Neue&family=Lora:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;1,400&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        try {
          var t = localStorage.getItem('cc-theme');
          if (!t) t = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: light)').matches ? 'light' : 'dark';
          document.documentElement.dataset.theme = t;
        } catch (e) { document.documentElement.dataset.theme = 'dark'; }
      })();
    </script>
    <style>
    /* ─── Reset & Base ─── */
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

    :root {
      --bg:       #0D0D0D;
      --text:     #F0EDE6;
      --amber:    #F5A623;
      --cyan:     #00C2CC;
      --muted:    #888884;
      --divider:  #1E1E1E;
      --panel:    #111111;
      --col:      680px;
    }

    :root[data-theme="light"] {
      --bg:       #F6F2E9;
      --text:     #171410;
      --amber:    #A96F00;
      --cyan:     #00747C;
      --muted:    #6E685C;
      --divider:  #DCD3BE;
      --panel:    #FFFDF8;
    }

    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }

    body {
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: 'Lora', Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.75;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      transition: background .3s ease, color .3s ease;
    }

    /* ─── Grain overlay ─── */
    body::before {
      content: '';
      position: fixed;
      inset: 0;
      pointer-events: none;
      z-index: 1000;
      opacity: .035;
      background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg viewBox='0 0 256 256' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Cfilter id='noise'%3E%3CfeTurbulence type='fractalNoise' baseFrequency='0.9' numOctaves='4' stitchTiles='stitch'/%3E%3C/filter%3E%3Crect width='100%25' height='100%25' filter='url(%23noise)'/%3E%3C/svg%3E");
      background-repeat: repeat;
      background-size: 256px 256px;
    }

    /* ─── Typography utilities ─── */
    .display { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif; letter-spacing: .04em; }
    .mono    { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }

    a { color: var(--amber); }

    /* ─── Theme switcher ─── */
    .theme-toggle {
      position: fixed;
      top: 1.25rem;
      right: 1.5rem;
      z-index: 1002;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .65rem;
      letter-spacing: .12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
      background: transparent;
      border: 1px solid var(--divider);
      padding: .5rem .9rem;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: color .2s, border-color .2s;
    }
    .theme-toggle:hover { color: var(--text); border-color: var(--muted); }

    /* ─── Layout ─── */
    .container {
      max-width: var(--col);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 2rem;
    }

    /* ─── Scroll animation ─── */
    .reveal {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(24px);
      transition: opacity .7s ease, transform .7s ease;
    }
    .reveal.visible {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
    }

    /* ─── Divider line ─── */
    hr.section-break {
      border: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--divider);
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       HERO
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    #hero {
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: flex-start;
      padding: 6rem 2rem 4rem;
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      position: relative;
    }

    #hero .hero-title {
      font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif;
      font-size: clamp(5rem, 15vw, 11rem);
      line-height: .9;
      letter-spacing: .02em;
      color: var(--text);
      animation: titleCut .5s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both;
      animation-delay: .1s;
    }

    #hero .hero-subtitle {
      font-family: 'Lora', serif;
      font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.4rem);
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
      font-style: italic;
      animation: titleCut .5s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both;
      animation-delay: .3s;
    }

    #hero .hero-byline {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .75rem;
      color: var(--amber);
      letter-spacing: .12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
      animation: titleCut .5s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both;
      animation-delay: .5s;
    }

    #hero .hero-cta {
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
      display: flex;
      gap: 1rem;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      animation: titleCut .5s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both;
      animation-delay: .65s;
    }

    @keyframes titleCut {
      from { opacity: 0; clip-path: inset(0 100% 0 0); }
      to   { opacity: 1; clip-path: inset(0 0% 0 0); }
    }

    /* ─── Scroll indicator ─── */
    .scroll-hint {
      position: absolute;
      bottom: 2.5rem;
      left: 2rem;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .65rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      letter-spacing: .1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: .6rem;
    }
    .scroll-hint::before {
      content: '';
      display: block;
      width: 30px;
      height: 1px;
      background: var(--muted);
    }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       CHAPTERS
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    .chapter {
      padding: 6rem 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--divider);
    }

    .chapter-label {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .7rem;
      color: var(--amber);
      letter-spacing: .15em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    }

    .chapter-number {
      font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif;
      font-size: 7rem;
      line-height: 1;
      color: var(--divider);
      position: absolute;
      right: 0;
      top: -1rem;
      pointer-events: none;
      user-select: none;
    }

    .chapter-header {
      position: relative;
    }

    .chapter-title {
      font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif;
      font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem);
      line-height: 1.05;
      letter-spacing: .03em;
      color: var(--text);
      margin-bottom: 3rem;
    }

    /* Pull quotes */
    blockquote {
      border-left: 2px solid var(--amber);
      margin: 2.5rem 0;
      padding: .75rem 0 .75rem 1.75rem;
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      font-style: italic;
      color: var(--text);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    blockquote cite {
      display: block;
      margin-top: .75rem;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .65rem;
      font-style: normal;
      color: var(--muted);
      letter-spacing: .1em;
    }

    /* Body copy spacing */
    .chapter p { margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
    .chapter p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    /* Node definitions */
    .node-title {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .8rem;
      color: var(--cyan);
      letter-spacing: .12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin: 2.5rem 0 .4rem;
    }

    /* System map / prompt panel */
    .system-map-wrap {
      margin: 3rem 0;
      border: 1px solid var(--divider);
      background: var(--panel);
      padding: 1.75rem;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .88rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .system-map-wrap .ph { color: var(--amber); }

    /* ─── Node pulse animation ─── */
    .node-dot {
      display: inline-block;
      width: 6px;
      height: 6px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--cyan);
      margin-right: .5rem;
      vertical-align: middle;
      animation: pulse 2.5s ease-in-out infinite;
    }

    @keyframes pulse {
      0%, 100% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1); }
      50%       { opacity: .3; transform: scale(.7); }
    }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       BUTTONS
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    .essay-cta {
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
    }

    .btn {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .8rem;
      letter-spacing: .12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--amber);
      border: 1px solid var(--amber);
      padding: .75rem 1.75rem;
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: background .2s, color .2s;
    }
    .btn:hover {
      background: var(--amber);
      color: var(--bg);
    }

    /* Stat line (proof entries) */
    .statline {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .7rem;
      color: var(--amber);
      letter-spacing: .15em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-bottom: .75rem;
    }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       THE ASK
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    #ask {
      padding: 8rem 0 6rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--divider);
    }

    #ask .container {
      max-width: 540px;
    }

    #ask .chapter-label {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    #ask p {
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    #ask p:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 0; }

    .contact-links {
      margin-top: 3rem;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .contact-link {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .8rem;
      letter-spacing: .1em;
      color: var(--amber);
      text-decoration: none;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: .6rem;
      transition: opacity .2s;
    }

    .contact-link::after {
      content: '→';
    }

    .contact-link:hover { opacity: .7; }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       FOOTER
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    footer {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--divider);
      padding: 3rem 2rem;
      text-align: center;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .65rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      letter-spacing: .08em;
      line-height: 2;
    }

    footer a {
      color: var(--muted);
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    footer a:hover { color: var(--text); }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       RESPONSIVE
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      body { font-size: 16px; }
      #hero { padding: 5rem 1.5rem 3rem; }
      .chapter { padding: 4rem 0; }
      .chapter-number { font-size: 5rem; right: 1.5rem; }
    }
    .method-video {
      margin-top: 2rem;
      padding: 1.25rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--divider);
      background: var(--panel);
    }
    .method-video h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; }
    .method-video button {
      margin-top: .75rem;
      padding: .65rem .9rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--muted);
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font: inherit;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    .method-video :focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--cyan); outline-offset: 3px; }
    .method-video iframe {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
      min-height: 200px;
      margin-top: .75rem;
      border: 0;
    }
    .method-video .watch-link { margin-top: .75rem; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>

    <button class="theme-toggle" id="themeToggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch colour theme">Light</button>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         HERO
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="hero">
      <h1 class="hero-title">CLAIM<br />CHECKER</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">An open method for verifying public claims against documented evidence.</p>
      <p class="hero-byline mono">TeamBotics Inc. · MIT Licence</p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/Teambotics-Inc/claim-checker">View the repository</a>
        <a class="btn" href="#ch03">Apply the method</a>
      </div>
      <span class="scroll-hint">Scroll</span>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         01 — WHAT IT CHECKS
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch01">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">01 / Scope</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">Scope</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p>Claim Checker applies to public claims that can be assessed against a documented record.</p>
          <p>The repository provides a standard and procedures for AI-assisted claim verification. It is not a hosted service.</p>
          <p>Statements from the subject form part of the record. Repetition does not constitute independent corroboration.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         02 — HOW IT WORKS
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch02">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">02 / The method</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">Verification Procedure</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Claim capture</p>
          <p>Record the exact wording, figures, date, speaker and source before analysis.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Evidence and citations</p>
          <p>Prefer primary sources. Cite only sources directly examined. Treat multiple accounts derived from the same source as one source.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Testing and counterevidence</p>
          <p>Apply the eight tests, including harm and proportionality. For each provisional verdict, document the search for counterevidence and its result.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Verdict classification</p>
          <p>Assign one verdict per claim: Confirmed, Partially corroborated, Self-reported only, Unverifiable by design, or Contradicted. Do not assign numerical scores. “Unverifiable by design” does not imply deception.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Independent validation</p>
          <p>A reviewer or second agent who did not produce the audit must verify the verdicts, harm assessment, reply record and conflict declaration. Disclose any relationship with the subject, including a personal dispute.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Right of reply</p>
          <p>Provide the subject with the exact claims and proposed verdicts. Allow 14 days for a response before publication. Publish any response with the audit. Record non-response without treating it as an admission.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="method-video" id="method-video">
          <h3>Method walkthrough</h3>
          <p>Overview of the published verification procedure.</p>
          <div data-player>
            <button type="button" aria-describedby="method-video-privacy" hidden>Load the YouTube player</button>
          </div>
          <p id="method-video-privacy" hidden>The player connects to YouTube only after activation.</p>
          <p class="watch-link"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6NeRnEJCf2I">View the walkthrough on YouTube</a></p>
        </div>
        <script is:inline>
          (function () {
            const walkthrough = document.getElementById('method-video');
            const player = walkthrough.querySelector('[data-player]');
            const button = player.querySelector('button');
            const privacyNote = document.getElementById('method-video-privacy');
            button.addEventListener('click', function () {
              const frame = document.createElement('iframe');
              frame.title = 'Claim Checker method walkthrough';
              frame.referrerPolicy = 'strict-origin-when-cross-origin';
              frame.allow = 'encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; fullscreen';
              frame.allowFullscreen = true;
              frame.tabIndex = 0;
              frame.src = 'https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/6NeRnEJCf2I';
              player.replaceChildren(frame);
              privacyNote.hidden = true;
              frame.focus();
            }, { once: true });
            privacyNote.hidden = false;
            button.hidden = false;
          })();
        </script>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         03 — USE IT
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch03">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">03 / Application</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">Applying the Method</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p><strong>1. Submit the claim and source.</strong> Use the following prompt with an AI agent that can inspect source material:</p>

          <div class="system-map-wrap">Apply the Claim Checker standard at <span class="ph">github.com/Teambotics-Inc/claim-checker</span> to <span class="ph">[exact claim and publication source]</span>. Follow the repository’s AGENTS.md.</div>

          <p><strong>2. Conduct and validate the audit.</strong> Apply the standard, document the evidence and arrange independent review. The method is free; any usage charges depend on the AI provider.</p>

          <p><strong>3. Review the outputs.</strong> The method produces a claim ledger, a <a href="https://storyteller.teambotics.app/"><strong>StoryTeller</strong></a> presentation and ranked follow-up questions.</p>

          <p>Each output identifies the agent, method version, dates and human reviewer. Without human review, label it <em>Unreviewed draft</em>. Independent audits are not TeamBotics findings. The publisher is responsible for publication.</p>

          <div class="essay-cta">
            <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/Teambotics-Inc/claim-checker">Open the repository</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         04 — PROOF
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch04">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">04 / Published examples</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">Published Examples</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="statline">247 tests · 32 deployments · 3 passes</p>
          <p class="node-title" style="margin-top:0"><span class="node-dot"></span><a href="https://frontdoor.teambotics.app" style="color:inherit">Operation Front Door</a></p>
          <p>The investigation tested candidate-facing hiring assistants at 64 employers using eight standard questions. It identified 32 confirmed Paradox deployments. None of the tested assistants described the role associated with its application. The investigation includes transcripts, scores and methodology.</p>
          <p><a href="https://frontdoor.teambotics.app">Read the investigation</a></p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="statline">16 claims · 2 validators · correction published</p>
          <p class="node-title" style="margin-top:0"><span class="node-dot"></span>Ground News</p>
          <p>Sixteen public claims about scale, bias ratings and funding were checked against primary sources and independently validated. The corrected tally was published with the analysis, presented in <a href="https://storyteller.teambotics.app/">StoryTeller</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="statline">16 exchanges · October 23, 2026 · verbatim</p>
          <p class="node-title" style="margin-top:0"><span class="node-dot"></span><a href="https://escapedboardy.teambotics.app" style="color:inherit">Escaped Boardy</a></p>
          <p>The published exchanges document an AI agent’s responses to questions about its company’s public claims. The dialogue is reproduced verbatim.</p>
          <p><a href="https://escapedboardy.teambotics.app">Read the exchanges</a></p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         05 — WHO IT'S FOR
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch05">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">05 / Intended users</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">Intended Users</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p>The method is intended for journalists, researchers, analysts and others who need to verify public claims.</p>
          <p>TeamBotics publishes its own audits under the Claim Checker name, with named editorial oversight. Independent users retain responsibility for their publications.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         06 — INDEPENDENCE & FUNDING
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch06">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">06 / Independence &amp; funding</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">Funding and Editorial Control</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p><strong>TeamBotics Inc.</strong>, a federally incorporated Canadian company, develops and funds Claim Checker. TeamBotics discloses no external funding, sponsorship or advertising. Claim Checker generates no revenue.</p>
          <p><strong>Nikhil Khedkar</strong> holds editorial control and is accountable for TeamBotics publications. See <a href="https://github.com/Teambotics-Inc/claim-checker/blob/main/docs/FUNDING-AND-ORGANISATION.md">Funding and organisation</a> for the full disclosure.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         07 — STANDARDS & OPEN FILES
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch07">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">07 / Standards</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">Editorial Standards</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Verifiable records</p>
          <p>Support findings with independently inspectable records, such as source captures, transcripts, version history and file hashes.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Quotation and context</p>
          <p>Quote the subject verbatim and in context. Publish the full exchange when it supports a finding.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Scope of findings</p>
          <p>Assess documented claims, records and system behaviour. Publish responses from the subject with the audit.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Corrections</p>
          <p>Publish corrections with the same prominence as the affected finding. See the <a href="https://frontdoor.teambotics.app/#corrections-log">Operation Front Door corrections log</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
